{"skill":{"slug":"scrapling-official","displayName":"Scrapling Official Skill"},"version":{"version":"0.5.0","createdAt":1792273592820,"changelog":"Version 0.5.0 introduces updated browser session handling and simplifies browser scraping options.\n\n- Added new browser session example (examples/02_browser_session.py)\n- Removed dynamic session example and deprecated fetching documentation\n- Updated CLI to use a unified \"fetch\" command for browser automation and anti-bot protection\n- Improved documentation for usage, CLI commands, and adaptive scraping\n- Revised references and examples to match new usage patterns and removed outdated details","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"LICENSE.txt","size":1499,"sha256":"5c782ef0346e4fbfe0dc76fd435f181a0f1e4a1a7a6b13c169c6e74314ff5964","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":25980,"sha256":"c6ea3753922e1c21669139ebf60a989499f326c10879257ab958c258386ed088","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"examples/01_fetcher_session.py","size":853,"sha256":"05fdb45c20a304f0fc8c979eabe7eb78b467951219be7b0a6a45d44c05b3ff68","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"examples/02_browser_session.py","size":954,"sha256":"786c2925550d36f0cfb84c0d53736ada24e7a5b6c0e0ad3f043a46d27a0dee33","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"examples/03_stealthy_session.py","size":952,"sha256":"a461dd666b82ce478e4bfdb966724d1c1b8807a3a10ce6b918d449c4d553bd4d","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"examples/04_spider.py","size":1941,"sha256":"2a899a24ebc827bec0b395f60d276813a99d27575255d28ede30e2cce38beac7","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"examples/README.md","size":1375,"sha256":"b965495f4d620dea8d4e988df1d3b6b8c6589019c239c2f2afc3a2b6b8634871","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/building-rag-systems.md","size":4934,"sha256":"6caf201c1e3bc55071f950457db8a40b93afb3395de98c435e30a426b8055a99","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/fetching/choosing.md","size":6447,"sha256":"a2aeeca0f256e2ded491311c5b1e8f90a5108637d12c999760ea9aac74c27e45","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/fetching/static.md","size":17626,"sha256":"782785aeec3abb641a659f889f3608d0e3d26a288ba9ff1587846fd1b32eb836","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/fetching/stealthy.md","size":35160,"sha256":"616a1b03bbf0e4065129ea3b6290e69653a8f0896c275976d987a1cae80e2681","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/integrations/scrapy.md","size":2985,"sha256":"911f5524b6cb8a5cf36f6971a7794b158912cbf1afcf40f51b888a539b51186d","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/mcp-server.md","size":26567,"sha256":"946e7b7093a037ddc6cda3fcd7fc9589d61f256a82fd9775c4895789854d4079","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/migrating_from_beautifulsoup.md","size":12646,"sha256":"b168e29be6eb94dcb442611e003f3dc74b87a4702f631d6baef220c1400d9a48","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/parsing/adaptive.md","size":12777,"sha256":"ca20857787e826ff380ca6c4e9483156c3f8feecd8e2285f8a9c630330481bcb","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/parsing/main_classes.md","size":28470,"sha256":"d7096792810392e97d2b9f6a8c06c999944badcc935d6da73f1eec2a839bab3c","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/parsing/selection.md","size":24754,"sha256":"1f558ce3162d2e24f19919c11fc2600b7d2515958ddc6cf051a1bc55ca0695de","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/advanced.md","size":18923,"sha256":"279d0fffed34b1ed1020e458c8dbce54b0576a9eb1bbeb594c611412b698e980","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/architecture.md","size":7448,"sha256":"ac24904d1bc4867fc51656456ade695e6c2245ac34278612aa0f1a7548ae6cc9","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/generic-templates.md","size":12419,"sha256":"18177ecb7fe26a974bc7fb9cc0d20411f98e3e92dc7f18da78ca504361e14b11","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/getting-started.md","size":7260,"sha256":"bb339e385338bf4fe3ed9cb72c75f4982b245311f28d607dc3290af00722d069","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/platform-templates.md","size":3306,"sha256":"0f557e46385d218b4c7976ea6763b0bb948fa2dc453b8bbf3ef33f07bf2fe88c","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/proxy-blocking.md","size":9075,"sha256":"cdb56ac5564cc0a9556f947c050a4adcb5b8f8b6c6f8a4a269310315eec91c6f","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/requests-responses.md","size":8988,"sha256":"c238afb9ab0f6f513deb68583cff2dfe8197b2e26441f717f0a38d6885404cab","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"references/spiders/sessions.md","size":9750,"sha256":"ab92cc48e882f1bdebc76cffe8304ab74e9a003de1908e29d1312fa25800e6a1","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2254,"sha256":"f8a974b113d407b6996808f79cd41445ed8805fefe1e03c82e29fbe48a1bcc43","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1792274195984,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"702c4f99aedb5cb9e753ba1a538c1e2a7c4fe16f1f63620d11daeca045ba1b8a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/702c4f99aedb5cb9e753ba1a538c1e2a7c4fe16f1f63620d11daeca045ba1b8a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1792273907451},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":96,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":107,"checkedAt":1792274195984},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a disclosed web-scraping skill with powerful browser and anti-bot features, but the artifacts are coherent with that purpose and I found no hidden or malicious behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Python, browser automation, network access, cookies, proxy settings, and optional MCP server exposure are proportionate for a scraping framework. The MCP reference documents authentication and warns against unauthenticated network exposure.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation uses pip plus Scrapling's browser installer, and optional Docker commands. The Docker examples use mutable images including latest, so users should pin versions or digests, but no hidden installer, autorun hook, or bundled malicious code was found in the skill artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Invocation guidance is broad for scraping and crawl/code-generation tasks, but the instructions stay within that domain and include guardrails to scrape only authorized content, respect robots.txt and ToS, avoid paywalls/auth bypass without permission, and avoid personal or sensitive data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Persistence is user-directed and documented: browser sessions can remain open, state files can save cookies/local storage, network history can be retained within a session, and spiders can write checkpoints or development caches. The docs warn to close sessions and not ship development caching enabled.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill is explicitly for Scrapling web scraping, including HTTP requests, stealth browser automation, JavaScript rendering, API capture, spiders, proxies, and Cloudflare handling; these are high-capability features but are disclosed and aligned with the stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you intentionally need a powerful scraping/browser automation tool. Pin package or Docker versions where possible, scrape only sites you are authorized to access, avoid passing real cookies or proxy credentials unless necessary, clear local state/caches when done, and do not expose the MCP HTTP server without authentication and TLS.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Network-capable scraping and browser automation are central to the skill. The artifact does not define a narrow tool-permission block, but the behavior is openly documented rather than hidden.\n[SQP-1] expected: The broad routing language maps to scraping, crawling, extraction, and scraping-code help. That breadth increases user responsibility but remains purpose-aligned.\n[RP1] unexpected: The optional Docker commands are not pinned to immutable digests or fixed reviewed versions. This is supply-chain hygiene guidance, not evidence of malicious behavior in the reviewed artifact.\n[SQP-2] expected: Writing fetched content, spider outputs, checkpoints, and caches is expected for scraping workflows. The artifact favors temp-file cleanup in the CLI notes and documents cache/state behavior, though users should choose safe output paths.\n[P9] expected: The whitespace findings correspond to wide Markdown tables and long documentation lines. Manual review found no concealed instructions or prompt-injection payload hidden behind the spacing.\n[TM3] expected: Development-mode caching is disclosed as local response replay for spider development, with warnings that it never expires and should not be shipped enabled.\n[SQP-2] expected: Anti-bot and Cloudflare-solving examples are an advertised scraping feature. They are sensitive capabilities, but the skill also includes authorization, robots.txt, ToS, paywall, authentication, and sensitive-data guardrails.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1792274195984}}}}}